	(text "Module: the magnetics and RJ45 are on the carrier (J1: ETH_TXP/N, ETH_RXP/N, ETH_LED1/2).\nThe PHY is clocked by the module oscillator on XTAL1/CLKIN (SYS_CLK); XTAL2 open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.828 23.114 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3500b828-3cab-50c2-9413-07fb2af0a5fb")
	)
	(text "Ethernet 10/100, RMII (untrusted from the RMII pins outward)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 19.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "36ae5790-b88e-533d-ba3b-59c26f69c3fa")
	)
	(text "Notes\n1. LAN8742A (LAN8720A fits the same footprint). REF_CLK out mode: LED2/nINTSEL pulled low, so the PHY\n   makes the 50 MHz RMII clock from the 25 MHz module oscillator on XTAL1/CLKIN (check REF_CLK out mode\n   with an external clock in the LAN8742A data sheet) rather than a crystal and nINT is not available.\n2. Straps left at their internal defaults: MODE[2:0] = 111 (auto-negotiate, all modes), PHYAD0 = 0,\n   REGOFF = 0 (internal 1.2 V regulator on, VDDCR is its output).\n3. ETH_RST_N has a pull-down: the PHY stays in reset until the loader releases it under the network\n   policy, and during FPGA configuration.\n4. LEDs are active high in this strap setting. Check the HR911105A LED polarity against its data sheet.\n5. A medical product needs a magnetics / isolation grade to IEC 60601-1 (open item A6); PoE is not provided."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4c7c5fa6-8b7b-5ff1-8a95-b615757c4279")
	)
	(text "VDDIO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 84.328 49.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7a53d6a1-5073-5ab8-b239-5dabd7a84042")
	)
	(text "VDDA_PHY: analog supply. The magnetics centre taps are fed on the carrier"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 60.706 0)
		(effects
